cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CheckWork in academic work, please cite the APNet '26 paper."
title: "CheckWork: Enabling Trace-Driven Analysis of Checkpointing Overhead in Distributed ML Training"
abstract: >
  CheckWork is an open-source framework that generates checkpoint-aware Chakra
  execution traces by augmenting synthetic training DAGs (produced by MLSynth)
  with checkpoint operations. The resulting traces can be replayed in any
  Chakra-compatible full-stack simulator (e.g. ASTRA-sim 2.0) to study how
  checkpointing strategies interact with compute, communication, parallelism,
  topology, and storage --- without requiring access to a physical GPU cluster.
